1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:08,830
Edited with FFmpeg, then shared.

2
00:00:08,830 --> 00:00:17,070
What tags are still inside?

3
00:00:17,070 --> 00:00:27,230
Title, artist, comment, location, handler name.

4
00:00:27,230 --> 00:00:40,780
Two readers: ffprobe, and a raw byte search.

5
00:00:40,780 --> 00:00:47,030
Plain re-encode: all five kept.

6
00:00:47,030 --> 00:00:53,280
-c copy: all five kept.

7
00:00:53,280 --> 00:00:59,160
-map_metadata -1: all five gone.

8
00:00:59,160 --> 00:01:05,030
Re-encode and -c copy agree.

9
00:01:05,030 --> 00:01:11,970
Left behind: an encoder tag, Lavf.

10
00:01:11,970 --> 00:01:16,590
-fflags +bitexact drops it.

11
00:01:16,590 --> 00:01:23,880
Not tested: real phone files, GPS tracks.

12
00:01:23,880 --> 00:01:31,170
Check the output before you share it.

13
00:01:31,170 --> 00:01:37,000
Kept by default. Removed on purpose.

14
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:43,800
Not tested: real phone files, other containers.
